In article <12237@pt.cs.cmu.edu> hairston@henry.ECE.CMU.EDU (David Hairston) writes:
>[prb@chinet.chi.il.us (Paul Botts) writes:]
>[] Here's a question for all you veteran demigods in the audience: when you
>[] get a wish, what do you wish for? How does your "wish list" vary with
>[] your characters/dungeon level/whatever? And how many ways are their to
>[] get wishes (I know of three: wand of wishing, magic lamp, fountain)?
>
>my 1st wish invariably is: a blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail

I never wish for dragon scale mail, because the armor will
periodically polymorph you into that color of dragon, causing you tear
out of your cloak (and hawiian shirt if you have one), so in other
words, combining a cloak of magic resistance with other armor will
yield a higher AC then gray dragon scale mail.

I generally only wish for things that I plan on finishing the game
(i.e. ascending) with, and generally things that can't be obtained
easily elsewhere. Although debatable, I would say that the best set of
armor/weapons/useful items one can have is:

*** Small chance for spoilers in discussion ahead ***

Weapons:
  a blessed broadsword named Stormbringer
    I'd choose this one over Mjollnir because it also will protect against
    drain level, which is useful when suddenly metting that vampire lord when
    you were playing around with a nurse.)
  (Excalibur obtained from a fountain is a close second because it also
   protects against level drain and is always rustproofed.)
  (A blessed athame is also very useful to have in that you can engrave
   Elbereth and not have it rub out for a while.)
Armor:
  a blessed elven-mithril coat
    Gives AC -5, and can be enchanted when up to +5 without evaporating.
    As good as [crystal] plate mail, but is much lighter and always rustproof.
  a blessed cloak of magic resistance
    This is the only other way I know of besides gray dragon scale mail to get
    magic resistance, which is why I'd choose this over, say cloak of
    displacement.
  a blessed hawiian shirt
    This is a unique piece of armor and is the only thing that will allow a
    character to have 7 pieces of armor on at once.
  a blessed shield of reflection
    Reflection is a vital intrinsic, which protects you from getting your
    scrolls burned by dragon breath and from running into pesky floating eyes.
    Don't obtain reflection from the amulet, save the amulet for live-saving!
    The shield also gives AC -2 even while unenchanted.
  a blessed pair of gauntlets of dexterity
    I'd choose this over gauntlets of power because a strength of 18/** is
    just about as good.
  a blessed helm of brilliance
    Although not as good AC as say a hard hat is, when enchanted it will
    allow you to cast spells with little difficulty and gets lots of stuff from
    your God when you #pray. I once has an Int of 24 and was able to cast
    genocide without even hearing "This spell is starting to being overused."
    An helm of telepathy can be faked with a blindfold and a f.e. corpse.
  a blessed pair of speed boots
    Increases your speed from 1.3x to 2x, which is a significant advantage
    even if you already "are fast". You can hit a monster, step back, he'll
    follow you on his turn, and you can hit him again! Water-walking boots
    are also good (and safe), but can be faked with a ring of levitation.
Rings:
  a blessed ring of levitation
    good for crossing water and #dipping stuff into it. Combine it with the
    athame and levitate over your Elbereth and kick butt.
  a blessed ring of teleport control
    Combine it with a nymph/leprechaun corpse and you can ^T away from trouble.
    Vital for getting down into hell to go after the Wiz. If playing Wizard,
    don't need it because you get tele. con. intrinsicly at Xp level 17.
    (Tengu corpses rarely ever give the intrinsic.)
  (I don't like using rings of conflict because I don't get the Xp. If I can't
   take on the monsters myself I'm too deep and shouldn't be on the level.)
  (All the intrinsic rings can be faked from corpses/wands/potions.)
Wands:
  a blessed wand of polymorph
    almost everything in this list can be obtained from one or two zaps on
    a large poly-pile.
Tools (in rough order of importance):
  a blessed blindfold
    Combine with a floating eye corpse and see where all the monster on the
    level are. Worth wishing for! (Try to start the game with one if you can.)
  a blessed unicorn horn
    Vital. Can immediately cure blindness, hallucination, confusion, stunning,
    and is useful for making water. Also rustproof but requires two hands.
  a blessed pick-axe
    Useful for the mazes and for robbing shops, vaults, statues, making pits
    for unexpecting monsters to fall into, etc.
  a blessed bag of holding
    To carry all of your junk around with you and all those dilithium crystals
    when leaving for the endgame. Make sure it doesn't get cursed, though.
  a mirror
    Combine it with telepathy to know when you are approaching Medusa/the Wiz.
  a blessed tinning kit
    Good for when satiated and you have a wraith corpse right in front of you.
  a skeleton key
    Open those chests and shopkeeper's doors. Lighter than a lock pick.
  a magic marker
    Make you own enchant armor/genocide scrolls. (If playing wizard, try to
    start with one.)

I generally only would with for things in the above list - once of got
all of the above, then I really don't need wishes anymore and just
wish for a bunch of cursed scrolls of genocide. Never wish for a
unicorn horn/pick-axe/mirror, too many monsters carry them around.
Blindfolds/ keys/magic markers appear somewhat often, especially if
you have a polypile. Make yourself Excalibur once you find a long
sword. If I've made it to dlvl 15-20 and still don't have a poly wand,
I'll wish for one. If chaotic, one can get Stormbringer without too
much trouble because there are only 3 chaotic weapons. If I'm on
dungeon level 10-15 I'd probably wish for the shield of reflection -
it's pretty rare, even for poly-piles, and of course one blast from an
orange dragon or a bump into a f.e. and your game is saved in
bones.xx.Z. Another good choice at this level is the magic resistance
cloak, those magic traps can summon a bunch of nasties, and a
polymorph trap can nuke your armor. If I get a wish *really* early in
the game, I'd probably wish for Stormbringer (or Mjollnir if Chaotic)
just so I can be sure of surviving until level 10 when the game *does*
seem to get easier, or perhaps for speed boots. If I only have some
of the armor listed above, I will try to only enchant those pieces
when I read the enchant armor scrolls. Oh, and wish for weapons/armor
+2 and not +3, because you have a better chance of getting them and
it's easier from there to get to the +3/+5 limits for armor/weapons.

